1. Derived from ZCode's dynamic-workflow runtime
------------------------------------------------
dsh-dwf is an independent reimplementation of the dynamic-workflow feature of
ZCode (a Z.ai / Zhipu product). The following parts were produced by studying
ZCode's shipped runtime and are therefore derivative:

  - `src/guest/prelude.ts`     guest program prelude (facade bridge, stall
                               detection semantics)
  - `src/guest/channels.ts`    channel / future pipeline primitives
  - `src/guest/realm.ts`       deterministic realm restrictions
  - `src/journal/schema.ts`    journal table layout
  - `src/util/fnv1a.ts`        site-id hashing scheme
  - `src/engine/actor.ts`      actor/subagent option mapping
  - `assets/facade.d.ts`       script-facing facade declaration
  - `assets/guest-prelude.js`, `assets/guest-channel-future.js`
  - `assets/journal-schema.sql`

No ZCode source code is redistributed verbatim by intent; the files above are
rewritten for the DSH plugin contract. ZCode itself is a separate product and
is NOT licensed by this project — obtain ZCode from its vendor and under its
own terms. "ZCode" is used here only to describe provenance, not as a claim of
affiliation or endorsement.

2. Built on DeepSeek Harness (@deepseek-ai/*)
---------------------------------------------
dsh-dwf is a plugin for DeepSeek Harness 0.2.1-rc.3 and implements interfaces
published by the official packages (cordis, dsh-workflow, dsh-agent,
dsh-subagent, dsh-ptc-runtime, dsh-sandbox, dsh-tools, dsh-session,
schemastery and related). Those packages are governed by their own licenses;
this project claims no rights over them and redistributes none of them.

3. Ported patterns from Claude Code dynamic workflows
-----------------------------------------------------
The facade vocabulary and several workflow patterns were informed by the
publicly documented Claude Code dynamic-workflows feature. No code is copied
from it.

